# One chat, one board task

The person asks to look at a task on the GitHub board. Stay in this chat. Do not suggest a new chat and do not start an autonomous loop from files in `prompts/`.

1. Read `.cursor/agents/initializer.md` and the `board-task` skill. Bring back a description and a plan. Stop and wait.
2. After approval or edits, the evaluator moves that issue to `board:in-progress`. Then follow `.cursor/agents/coder.md` and the coder skills in this same chat.
3. Then follow `.cursor/agents/evaluator.md` and the `verify-task` skill in this same chat. If the check fails, the coder fixes that same task here.
4. When the check passes, the evaluator moves the card to `board:in-review` and opens the pull request. Stop there.

The person reviews the pull request, merges it, moves the card to `board:done`, and closes the issue. Do not do those four steps.

`TASK.md` is the product description. Take technical constraints from the agent skills. Do not add them to `TASK.md`.
